Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/unmarked/c/mLMmfVma_30/m/WgNciWv0QSIJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi all,

I am running open occ models like the following:  (fm30<- colext(~1, ~1, ~scale(warea), ~1, occ.umf))

Notice I am scaling the continuous covariate(warea) within the formula.  I saw in Richard's reply to a previous thread  (Model predictions when scaling covariates , from March 2011)  that when you use "predict" after a model such as this, the backtransformation/rescaling is already performed.  I want the backtransformed/original scale values for the extinction intercept and beta(warea)-- and don't know how to get those using predict?  I was using something like this (beta(warea) code only for brevity)  and receiving output that appeared to be backtransformed and unscaled:

 warea.ext<-backTransform(linearComb(fm30,type="ext",coefficients=c(0,1)))
> warea.ext
Backtransformed linear combination(s) of Extinction estimate(s)

 Estimate     SE LinComb (Intercept) scale(warea)
   0.0039 0.0134   -5.54           0            1

However, when compared to output from the model summary I noticed that while the parameter estimates are the same, the standard error estimates here do NOT correspond with the  backtransformed estimates I get from that output (see below).  The SEs are very different-- which method is correct (if either??).

Extinction (logit-scale):
             Estimate   SE     z P(>|z|)
(Intercept)     -4.32 2.33 -1.85  0.0639
scale(warea)    -5.54 3.46 -1.60  0.1092

> plogis(-5.54)
[1] 0.00391117    #same parameter estimate as above
> plogis(3.46)
[1] 0.969528       #DIFFERENT SE estimate from above

Thanks for any help with this!
Tamara Pandolfo

