hi Tamara,

this may not be very helpful, but: you can't directly compare the SE. In particular, you can't do plogis(SE_hat) ! I assume that one is on the logit scale and the other on the probabilty scale, but I never understood how one can get a "non-asymmetric" SE on the latter. After all, the SE is symmetric on the link scale of the analysis, which is the logit here, so how can one get a single SE for a backtransformed estimate ? That has always puzzled me in MARK also.

Regards  --  Marc

