in response to Marc's email:  Marc suggests that computing a confidence interval for the back-transformed parameter (i.e., on the probabiliy scale) based on the approximate standard error would be unappealing because it would be symmetric.  An alternative approach is to compute the confidence interval on the linear scale and then back-transform the endpoints.

